The Anchorage Group (TAG) Company Profile
The Anchorage Group (TAG) is a Malawian owned company dedicated to advancing commercial agriculture, value addition, food safety, and export market development. We work across the entire value chains from commercial production, agro-trading, processing, foos safety, and supporting farmer linkages with financial institutions and development partners for agriculture value chain development. 
TAG is also the sole certified distributor of Aflasafe in Malawi, approved by the International Institute of Tropical Agriculture (IITA). Aflasafe is a proven biocontrol product that reduces aflatoxin contamination in maize, sorghum, groundnuts, sesame, and millet, forming part of our integrated food safety and aflatoxin management system.
We operate in climate resilient high value chains such as soybeans, groundnuts, African bird’s eye chili, sorghum, sesame, cotton, and white haricot beans.
TAG focus areas
•	Premium offtake of aflatoxin compliant agricultural products and other commodities
•	Commercial agricultural production through Anchor Farm model and structured out grower scheme.
•	Export market development and international buyer linkages.
•	Agricultural value chain development and system strengthening
•	Inclusive farmer partnerships that improve productivity and incomes
•	Sustainable agricultural investment and agribusiness growth
•	Agricultural input distribution, including Aflasafe.
•	Commodity aggregation and trading
•	Farmer support programmes such as promoting sustainable agriculture practices, linking farmers to financial institutions and agriculture insurance
•	Food safety and aflatoxin management interventions
•	Agro processing and value addition
